* hello.a -- smoke test for the toolchain: a Code object that adds 1 to the
* user binary integer in stack level 1, in place.  #41h EVAL -> #42h.
* Uses no ROM entries.  D0 (RPL instruction pointer) is left untouched.
        NIBASC  \HPHP48-E\
        CON(5)  #02DCC          Code prolog (DOCODE)
        REL(5)  end             length of the code body
        A=DAT1  A               A = address of the object in level 1
        AD1EX                   D1 = object, A = saved stack pointer
        D1=D1+  10              skip prolog (02A4E) and length field (00015)
        C=DAT1  W               C = 64-bit value
        C=C+1   W
        DAT1=C  W
        AD1EX                   restore stack pointer
        A=DAT0  A               LOOP: continue with the next RPL object
        D0=D0+  5
        PC=(A)
end
